# Frontend component files

When creating a component or view, use a directory (not a single file) with these files:

- `index.tsx` — JSX, `useState`, `useEffect`, render
- `types.ts` — types only
- `helpers.ts` — non-trivial functions
- `styles.css` — all styles; no inline styles
- `constants.ts` — only when the component has many constants

Do not put types, helpers, or CSS in `index.tsx`. Do not use `style={{}}` or other inline styles.

Pattern (`types.ts`):

```ts
type Health = 'loading' | 'ok' | 'error'
```

```tsx
# BAD
function App() {
  const [health, setHealth] = useState('loading')
  return <p style={{ color: 'green' }}>{health}</p>
}

# GOOD
HealthView/
  index.tsx
  types.ts
  helpers.ts
  styles.css
  constants.ts   # only if needed
```
